# Transactions

> Status: Ready
> Priority: P0
> Depends On: Accounts, Categories
> Next Feature: Budgets

---

# Overview

Transactions are the core records of financial activity in Kin Finance.

Every Transaction records a financial event: money coming in (income), money going out (expense), or money moving between accounts (transfer). Income and expense Transactions are linked to an Account and a Category. Transfers link two Accounts (from → to) and have no Category.

In MVP, Transactions are simple (no split, no recurring). Both Owner and Member can create, edit, and delete Transactions freely. Every Transaction records who created and updated it.

---

# Goals

- Allow users to record income and expenses.
- Allow users to move money between accounts (transfers).
- Auto-update Account balance(s) on every transaction change.
- Track who created and updated each Transaction.

---

# Scope

## In Scope

- Create a Transaction (income, expense, or transfer).
- Edit a Transaction.
- Delete a Transaction.
- List Transactions with date filtering.
- Auto-update Account balance(s) on create/edit/delete.
- Record createdBy and updatedBy metadata.

## Out of Scope

- Split transactions (future).
- Recurring transactions (future).
- Attachments/receipts (future).
- Multi-currency (future).

